# App Code Patterns (Next.js + TypeScript)

## File Structure
- Use the App Router with `app/`; each route is a directory with `page.tsx`
- Use `layout.tsx` for shared layouts
- Place components in `app/_components/` (or co-locate with pages)

## Page & Layout Components
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for interactivity or browser APIs
- Export default functions with descriptive names; type props with interfaces
- Root layout: see [app/layout.tsx](mdc:spots-app/app/layout.tsx) — metadata, fonts, [app/globals.css](mdc:spots-app/app/globals.css)
- Auth / protected pages: see login and dashboard page patterns; Amplify UI where appropriate for auth flows

## Styling
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes; [app/app.css](mdc:spots-app/app/app.css) for app-specific styles
- CSS modules only when needed; mobile-first responsive layout

## Data Fetching
- Fetch in Server Components when possible
- Use `loading.tsx` / `error.tsx` for route loading and error boundaries
- Follow Next.js 15 App Router data-fetching patterns

## TypeScript Configuration
- Strict mode via [tsconfig.json](mdc:spots-app/tsconfig.json); import with `@/` path alias
- Define interfaces/types for props, API payloads, and domain models — prefer `unknown` over `any`

## Business Logic Types
- Prefer `*-business.ts` naming for domain types under `app/_lib/types/` (or equivalent)
- Export reusable types for services and hooks
- Type PRO-CTCAE / symptom structures strictly where they exist
- Amplify: import schema types from [amplify/data/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/data/resource.ts); use typed Data client `generateClient<Schema>()` when touching Amplify Data
- Type auth user fields and all REST request/response shapes for backend/REDCap APIs

## Hooks, State & Errors
- Type custom hook args, return values, and event handlers
- Type business state (symptoms, cart, search) explicitly
- Prefer typed errors / error boundaries for async and UI failure paths
